    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d172">

                <pb facs="0220" n="1054" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1054"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/9910</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Stovall</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-09-04T18:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 4, 1918, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2659. For Dresel [from War Trade Board]:</p>
                <p>No. 96. Plan for Swiss lists, Legation’s 4459, August 24, noon, your 132,<anchor
                        n="2" xml:id="d172-f1"/> approved. Have telegraphed Paris to urge French to
                    adopt. Shall take matter up with French High Commission here also.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
